# 04 — Migrate MLDPConfigurationWriter + MLDPPVMetadataWriter to BaseQueuedWriter

**Depends on**: `01-base-queued-writer` complete.
**Can run parallel with**: `02`, `03`.

## Goal

Both writers use simple single-threaded queues with low-volume payloads.
Migrating them to `BaseQueuedWriter` standardizes lifecycle and removes
hand-rolled thread boilerplate.

---

## MLDPConfigurationWriter

**Payload types**: `ConfigurationPayload`, `ConfigurationActivationPayload`
**Workers**: 1 (single-threaded RPC calls)
**Queue capacity**: 1000 (suggested default; low throughput)

### Item type

```cpp
struct ConfigItem {
    util::bus::IDataBus::EventBatch batch;  // carry full batch; processItem unpacks
};
```

Or store the variant payload directly if unpacking in `toItems()` is cleaner.

### Checklist

- [ ] Define `ConfigItem` inner struct
- [ ] `BaseQueuedWriter<ConfigItem>` as base
- [ ] `toItems()`: accept `ConfigurationPayload` OR `ConfigurationActivationPayload`;
  return 1-element vector; drop others silently
- [ ] `processItem()`: body of existing `workerLoop` minus dequeue/shutdown
  (`doSaveConfiguration` / `doSaveConfigurationActivation` calls stay)
- [ ] Remove `start()`, `stop()`, thread members
- [ ] `doStart()`: initialize gRPC stub / pool if needed
- [ ] `doStop()`: cleanup stubs

---

## MLDPPVMetadataWriter

**Payload type**: `SourceMetadataPayload`
**Workers**: 1
**Queue capacity**: 1000 (suggested default)

### Item type

```cpp
struct MetadataItem {
    std::string source;
    /* metadata fields extracted from SourceMetadataPayload */
};
```

### Checklist

- [ ] Define `MetadataItem` inner struct
- [ ] `BaseQueuedWriter<MetadataItem>` as base
- [ ] `toItems()`: accept `SourceMetadataPayload`; fan-out to one item per
  metadata entry if that matches existing `push()` logic; else one item per batch
- [ ] `processItem()`: body of existing `workerLoop` / `saveSourceMetadata`
- [ ] Remove `start()`, `stop()`, thread members
- [ ] `doStart()` / `doStop()`: gRPC pool init/reset

